  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "You read almost everything, but with rules.",
   "texto": [
    "In German, almost all letters are pronounced. What changes is some combinations.",
    "**ei** sounds «ai» (heiße) and **ie** sounds «i» long (Ye, wie). **eu** and **äu** sound «oi» (Freund).",
    "**sch** sounds «sh» (tschüss). **ch** sounds like a jota: soft after e, i (ich) and strong after a, o, u (auch).",
    "**w** sounds like a v (wie) and **v** sounds almost always «f» (vier). **z** sounds «ts» (zehn). **j** sounds «and» (ja).",
    "The **s** at the beginning of the word, before vowel, vibrates like a buzzing (Ye, sehr)."
   ]
  },
